#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129004 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "b776ff14-81d8-5e5d-8ea4-15969eb3904e" :question/math-academy-id "e-9816" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $\\mathbf{u}=(5\\mathbf{i} +2\\mathbf{j}) \\,\\textrm{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|5i+2j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/id #uuid "33aad515-8d28-57f4-8d3e-448eb905324c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9817" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0 \\, \\textrm{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $4\\mathbf{i}  \\, \\textrm{km/h},$ and when $t=3\\, \\textrm{h},$ the velocity of the particle is $(7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j})  \\, \\textrm{km/h}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = 4\\mathbf{i}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{v} = 7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\nt =3\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $\\mathbf{a}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 7i+15j & =4i+a(3) \\\\ 3i+15j & =3a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{3}(3i+15j) \\\\ a & =(i+5j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129006 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/id #uuid "bf9ee32f-b32c-5acc-90f7-c2daf10b2497" :question/math-academy-id "e-9818" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(\\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{s}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}^2,$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=5 \\, \\textrm{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = 2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j} .\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t = 5 \\, \\textrm{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(i-4j)+(2i+j)(5) \\\\  & =(i-4j)+(10i+5j) \\\\  & =(11i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Time when a Particle Reaches a Particular Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "e2aff165-10d7-5d4d-9058-a15121222ebe" :question/math-academy-id "e-9819" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}^2.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j})  \\, \\textrm{km/h}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{u} = -\\mathbf{i} -\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad\n\\mathbf{v} = 3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i+7j & =(-i-j)+(i+2j)t \\\\ 4i+8j & =(i+2j)t \\\\ 4i+8j & =ti+2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4=t \\\\ 8=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c27fa1b4-0e14-5062-bc9c-d6ebd2e1bdc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{67}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286002} {:answer/id #uuid "c281d91b-378b-517e-bd40-11cf26cf034f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{74}km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286003} {:answer/id #uuid "17235203-bcb1-57d2-b17c-e6167bb4e9cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286004} {:answer/id #uuid "99677049-6bd2-5607-86b4-c6a438a6bac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286005} {:answer/id #uuid "8b3e8003-471a-5049-9d47-1d103b431bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286006}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c281d91b-378b-517e-bd40-11cf26cf034f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{74}km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286003} :answer-field/id #uuid "e768317c-11c5-5c3b-a5d8-7c53fdd01cd3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286001}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "de06da58-c21f-5b57-9d0e-aa8b476e4cc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-136288" :question/problem "The initial velocity of a particle is $(5i-j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle after $2$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i+3j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i-j,\\,a=i+3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $2$ hours, the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(i+3j)(2) \\\\  & =(5i-j)+(2i+6j) \\\\  & =(7i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|7i+5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{74}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4672d49-ed68-5749-af07-6551eb7fbbe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i + 4j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126291} {:answer/id #uuid "246893e9-8f38-5719-90f9-e5359a2f8b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i - 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126292} {:answer/id #uuid "391f27a5-4c27-5b93-be93-463a8369ec52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i + 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126293} {:answer/id #uuid "5fea3226-571f-5dcb-86c8-5248838fabcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126294} {:answer/id #uuid "7c97e288-29da-529f-b1fe-9e0ff3367ca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4im/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "391f27a5-4c27-5b93-be93-463a8369ec52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i + 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126293} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccfed89d-b25d-5449-a46c-bd5f21d33670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d30498e-757c-511b-b142-9c3f837aad12" :question/math-academy-id "q-136289" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(-2i-8j)\\,\\text{m/s},$ and when $t=4\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $2i\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-2i-8j,\\,v=2i,\\,t=4,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 2i & =(-2i-8j)+a(4) \\\\ 4i+8j & =4a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}(4i+8j) \\\\  & =(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129416 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Time when a Particle Reaches a Particular Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d039f4a6-471f-5a6d-8c7b-7b6f20da9885" 