ligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}9=3t \\\\ 6=2t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=3\\,\\text{s}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Time when a Particle Reaches a Particular Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ea74266-5bac-53cd-b03b-84bdff94703d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126309} {:answer/id #uuid "ea5b82cb-f095-59bb-a0b0-67a7f9b378c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 1s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126310} {:answer/id #uuid "2ac0543b-c37c-567f-b5e7-61503aea764b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 3s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126311} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd52aef-a51f-551c-bf22-1e49ca7e6e66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 2s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126312} {:answer/id #uuid "43a4a3fa-a111-56e5-a3f3-1e0c2ee7489b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t = 4s" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ea74266-5bac-53cd-b03b-84bdff94703d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126309} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a952c76-2582-54e4-bf1a-64099c8e9ac8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126308}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf5bf00a-e492-5d4d-9f8a-0af5a0102f4d" :question/math-academy-id "q-136293" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i-2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=i-2j,\\,u=2i-5j,\\,v=3i-j\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can attempt to solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i-j & =(2i-5j)+(i-2j)t \\\\ i+4j & =(i-2j)t \\\\ i+4j & =ti-2tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=t \\\\ 4=-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286007 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d29dc2cf-7867-5d62-b135-439286b2d1b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.73\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286009} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d360c0-f552-57d5-be87-3ed97c4c98de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.65\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286010} {:answer/id #uuid "40150e22-5fae-514a-8ac8-69c1dd2ada3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6.31\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286011} {:answer/id #uuid "efb737a0-b2ac-5590-9b73-0a08d7ca82d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.39\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286012} {:answer/id #uuid "5da3556a-49d7-5bc9-98d1-22595e139586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.67\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286013}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efb737a0-b2ac-5590-9b73-0a08d7ca82d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.39\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286012} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fb9bcad-db5a-5f4f-b760-96a6e3e19056" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d9adc28-1eef-586b-9169-6940ecdacba5" :question/math-academy-id "q-136311" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the speed of the particle, rounding your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|2i-5j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+25} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29} \\\\  & ≈5.39\\,\\text{m/s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12aff03a-a111-5da4-a0a8-17249d4bb642" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.24\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286016} {:answer/id #uuid "962cc917-c5fc-5ff3-a7c7-e2a08a42dda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.87\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286017} {:answer/id #uuid "62ab45b6-a2b9-5bcd-aa2e-758226381f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.18\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286018} {:answer/id #uuid "bca70a85-c467-57a1-bbd5-6ce895bc091d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.68\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286019} {:answer/id #uuid "db3625a6-eede-5ea4-bf4b-d8cd4cb3ae80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.12\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286020}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db3625a6-eede-5ea4-bf4b-d8cd4cb3ae80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.12\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286020} :answer-field/id #uuid "50a5b134-5754-5040-86ca-52d65e9d5003" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ede10ea1-892c-5590-9caf-f40ffde6984b" :question/math-academy-id "q-136312" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=(i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle, rounding your answer to two decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|i+4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17} \\\\  & ≈4.12\\,\\text{km/h}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to two decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bb12dee-7aff-5e21-9d9f-a0b0d7971401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286023} {:answer/id #uuid "084f17c7-676c-5ae3-a07d-10ae445cc19a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286024} {:answer/id #uuid "ded465af-7bcf-5d15-b449-3570be3e20ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286025} {:answer/id #uuid "5739e4ce-61a5-5e20-bae7-5beb400e34d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286026} {:answer/id #uuid "78c253cb-6eb1-598d-bdc0-1552f436a278" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4bb12dee-7aff-5e21-9d9f-a0b0d7971401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286023} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2bb7b45-af36-51e4-9333-c41840f82a8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "732947d8-900a-567c-973c-5bad2bf95058" :question/math-academy-id "q-136315" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=-2i\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|-2i| \\\\  & =|-2| \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa1e67c-f0c4-5f3b-a608-9d968ee219dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286030} {:answer/id #uuid "109ff4aa-7a72-573d-bb58-8bee0cd6c0a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286031} {:answer/id #uuid "d25765ac-e1bf-59b8-ac73-d43fb3256175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286032} {:answer/id #uuid "4eb4953f-a40a-5977-a0a2-6ddf663e835b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286033} {:answer/id #uuid "08822315-57d1-54b2-8e55-efc8585b711d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4eb4953f-a40a-5977-a0a2-6ddf663e835b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286033} :answer-field/id #uuid "32b70a93-1f04-5125-bfaf-2ab682c16c06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b531cc0-4486-5687-827b-8217ae5fddb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-136320" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $u=-7j\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the speed of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =|-7j| \\\\  & =|-7| \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ea1127-0d81-5372-83dc-4603dbf19837" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10i-6j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286037} {:answer/id #uuid "cafb14a7-e8ba-5e2a-9056-82c84d03640c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286038} {:answer/id #uuid "e05dcb19-3698-5bc0-bfe2-4727ef012835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286039} {:answer/id #uuid "145bcf6d-dc64-57c7-8b8f-f7edc5e47682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7i-j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286040} {:answer/id #uuid "d98f03ca-2810-5253-ba0c-8c6444cd9e9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e05dcb19-3698-5bc0-bfe2-4727ef012835" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286039} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f630da0-d649-5baa-a7a5-cba3a7e9f50e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d910d63b-bba9-5d02-aaf7-5410fa0ed263" :question/math-academy-id "q-136337" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(5i-3j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i+2j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i-3j,\\,a=i+2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=2\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i-3j)+(i+2j)(2) \\\\  & =(5i-3j)+(2i+4j) \\\\  & =(7i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed6afabf-993e-53c3-95be-16ce64b79c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286044} {:answer/id #uuid "11c2dea5-4745-5c21-a8c6-72b625a0bc62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6i+24j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286045} {:answer/id #uuid "3d956f1f-d2ea-5b73-b5f0-9988adcb9189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286046} {:answer/id #uuid "529f2db0-06fd-575c-9517-aca9884bb38a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i+5j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286047} {:answer/id #uuid "31323204-e7e6-5b86-b598-d1c802af04d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11i+6j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed6afabf-993e-53c3-95be-16ce64b79c6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286044} :answer-field/id #uuid "0211f49b-01d6-5afb-a665-7801f6f16ba1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "475b8376-b64f-5b88-84dc-3087e08b2993" :question/math-academy-id "q-136341" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(-i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=6\\,\\text{h}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=-i+4j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=6\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(2i+j)(6) \\\\  & =(-i+4j)+(12i+6j) \\\\  & =(11i+10j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b613c9d1-0613-5f6a-b05e-ca23fe414135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286051} {:answer/id #uuid "8b1344ac-fb93-57b7-b128-3ee05cd48b9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17i+j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286052} {:answer/id #uuid "baaea489-308b-59fd-bff5-fcaf5b002b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(20i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286053} {:answer/id #uuid "a4c0acf5-9465-57e7-8062-efea4b5a540d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+4j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286054} {:answer/id #uuid "8369182c-65e6-501c-8d7b-844bfd18614e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8369182c-65e6-501c-8d7b-844bfd18614e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286055} :answer-field/id #uuid "7eaf27aa-c1d5-535e-a51d-33364ab0d312" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "334ab911-0f79-50ec-b4ac-385f83fb2702" :question/math-academy-id "q-136342" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(5i+j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $3j\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2},$ find the velocity of the particle when $t=4\\,\\text{h}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=5i+j,\\,a=3j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=4\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(5i+j)+(3j)(4) \\\\  & =(5i+j)+(12j) \\\\  & =(5i+13j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25feade-2661-524f-ac24-30e9dbde89dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286058} {:answer/id #uuid "b55538a5-958e-5cb9-95b1-dc04b61fba5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3j\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286059} {:answer/id #uuid "95cbb249-cfe6-5beb-9445-b74c3ebafa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286060} {:answer/id #uuid "a67db531-45c1-5334-97dd-f6b889f4a2c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6i\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286061} {:answer/id #uuid "fa05ba84-cb8e-5fef-b61b-b817a9b3aa6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95cbb249-cfe6-5beb-9445-b74c3ebafa39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286060} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3ac62b9-a8cd-50dd-b41f-5b469fc02c26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a260087-aef9-52a3-8b76-b4f416b4f142" :question/math-academy-id "q-136365" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(i-6j)\\,\\text{m/s},$ and when $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle is $(4i+3j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=i-6j,\\,v=4i+3j,\\,t=3,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 4i+3j & =(i-6j)+a(3) \\\\ 3i+9j & =3a \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{3}(3i+9j) \\\\  & =(i+3j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Time when a Particle Reaches a Particular Velocity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d27c544-66e5-543e-b587-bf4cf42e2ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286065} {:answer/id #uuid "677740a7-2bce-58e7-932d-82c5794e7e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=1\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286066} {:answer/id #uuid "d76df32d-5e0d-5b6d-b68a-700bb3ac68e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286067} {:answer/id #uuid "8fcb2589-33cd-5a36-af75-219ed665fb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286068} {:answer/id #uuid "7037984d-72d7-5b3c-b6f1-d6f745d389bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2\\,\\text{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d76df32d-5e0d-5b6d-b68a-700bb3ac68e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286067} :answer-field/id #uuid "08a68bf3-f888-5eea-b6bf-d5a97bd6d5e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286064}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c92bf72-1a37-50b1-9e0c-abea59db65f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-136407" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+7j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(2i-5j)\\,\\text{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3i+2j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\na=-i+7j,\\,u=2i-5j,\\,v=3i+2j\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can attempt to solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 3i+2j & =(2i-5j)+(-i+7j)t \\\\ i+7j & =(-i+7j)t \\\\ i+7j & =-ti+7tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=-t \\\\ 7=7t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "480753c5-0d0d-51c0-ba24-0967d975d9d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "480753c5-0d0d-51c0-ba24-0967d975d9d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286072} :answer-field/id #uuid "41a53f06-9530-5e4c-932f-df8d83e29d25" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286071} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5dc76c5-7c08-524e-ac92-045277e888c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5dc76c5-7c08-524e-ac92-045277e888c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286074} :answer-field/id #uuid "f43ecdae-9c55-5ad1-888d-320d8787776c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c160132d-20d0-59f1-aea1-6e3f6c75bcba" :question/math-academy-id "q-317176" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. The velocity of the particle equals $(-4i+9j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ both when $t=0\\,\\text{s}$ and $t=7\\,\\text{s}.$ What is the acceleration of the particle?\n\n$a=($\n{{field-1}}$\\,i$\n$+$\n{{field-2}}$\\,j\\,)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-4i+9j,\\,v=-4i+9j,\\,t=7\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $a,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -4i+9j & =(-4i+9j)+a(7) \\\\ 0 & =7a \\\\ a & =(0\\,i+0\\,j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286075 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1e27185-b104-5e3b-ae25-a98124f661d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286077} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e7f5bf-c6b4-5b7c-a165-781ce19a7f8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math}